WEBVTT

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:14.560
Wow.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:16.960
(STUDENTS MURMURING)

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:31.640
(SCOFFS)

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.160
You got to be kidding me.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.120
I'm so nervous!

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.320
Relax. It will be fine.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:37.920
-Good morning, students.
-(STUDENTS SHUSHING)

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.120
Welcome to Scaring 101.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.120
I am Professor Knight.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:45.840
Now I'm sure all of you
were the scariest monster in your town.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:49.280
Well, bad news, kids.
You're in my town now,

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.360
and I do not scare easily. (GASPS)

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.200
(STUDENTS MURMURING)

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:06.360
Dean Hardscrabble.
This is a pleasant surprise.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:10.800
She's a legend.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:14.400
She broke the all-time Scare Record
with the scream in that very can!

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:17.360
I don't mean to interrupt.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:19.040
I just thought I'd drop by

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:22.640
to see the terrifying faces
joining my program.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:23.520
(ALL MURMURING)

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:26.040
Well, I'm sure my students
would love to hear

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.000
a few words of inspiration.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.680
Inspiration? Very well.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:38.200
Scariness is the true measure
of a monster.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.680
If you're not scary

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:43.040
what kind of a monster are you?

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:48.120
It's my job to make
great students greater,

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:53.280
not make mediocre students
less mediocre.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:57.760
That is why at the end of the semester
there will be a final exam.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:04.080
Fail that exam and you are
out of the Scaring program.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:07.320
-(GASPS)
-(ALL MURMURING)

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:12.600
So, I should hope
you're all properly inspired.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.280
(STUDENTS GASP)

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:17.680
(MURMURING CONTINUES)

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:20.200
KNIGHT: All right. All right.

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:24.280
Who can tell me the properties
of an effective roar?

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:26.120
Yes?

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.880
There are actually five.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:31.120
Those include the roar's resonance,

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.320
the duration of the roar, and the...

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:34.680
-(ROARING)
-(ALL GASP)

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:38.920
Whoops. Sorry.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.880
I heard someone say "roar,"
so I just kind of went for it.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:43.840
Oh, excuse me, sorry.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.560
I didn't mean to scare you there.
Hey, how you doing?

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:48.400
Very impressive, Mister...

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.200
Sullivan. Jimmy Sullivan.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:51.600
Sullivan.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:53.800
Like Bill Sullivan, the Scarer?

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.640
Yeah. He's my dad.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.920
-(ALL MURMURING)
-He's a Sullivan!

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:01.320
I should have known.
I expect big things from you.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:04.040
Well, you won't be disappointed.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.480
Uh... I'm sorry. (STAMMERS)
Should I keep going?

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.000
No, no. Mr. Sullivan's covered it.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:10.360
(CLICKS TONGUE)

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:11.920
Huh.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.120
Everyone take out
your Scaring textbooks

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.080
and open them to chapter one.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:18.120
Hey, bub. Can I borrow a pencil?

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.840
I forgot all my stuff.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:23.000
Ah! All right. Yes.
There we go. That will get it.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:24.760
Mmm... Yeah.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:27.600
RANDY: Come on, Mike. It's a fraternity

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.680
and sorority party. We have to go!

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:32.240
If we flunk that Scaring final,
we are done.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:34.000
I'm not taking any chances.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.440
RANDY: You've got
the whole semester to study,

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.280
but this might be our only chance

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.120
to get in good with the cool kids.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.880
That's why I made these cupcakes.
Oops.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.920
(CHUCKLES) That could
have been embarrassing.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.760
When I'm a Scarer,
life will be a nonstop party.

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:47.040
Stay out of trouble, wild man.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.160
(CHUCKLES) Wild man.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:51.120
(CHUCKLES)

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.480
(GRUNTING)

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:00.600
(EXCLAIMS IN SURPRISE)

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:02.280
What the...

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:03.720
(SQUEALS)

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:06.000
-(SCREAMS)
-Archie!

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:07.480
(BOTH SCREAM)

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.040
Boo!

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:10.240
-Hey! What are you...
-(SHUSHING)

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:13.840
Wait... You're shushing me?
Hey! Hey! You can't...

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.360
(MUFFLED MUTTERING)

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:16.840
MONSTER 1: Where did he go?
MONSTER 2: He's dead meat.

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:19.400
-That guy's in big trouble.
-Yeah, he is.

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:21.560
MONSTER 3: Hey, guys! Over here!

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:22.880
(CHUCKLES)

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:24.360
-Fear Tech dummies.
-(MUFFLED PROTESTS)

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:26.240
-(GASPING)
-Oh, oh!

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:28.400
-Sorry about that, buddy.
-Why are you in my room?

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:29.600
Your room? This is my...

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.640
This is not my room.

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:33.840
Archie! Come here, boy.

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:35.000
-(MIMICS PIG)
-Archie?

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:37.200
Archie the Scare Pig.
He's Fear Tech's mascot.

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:38.760
-Why is it here?
-(SNIGGERING)

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:41.000
I stole it. Going to take it to the RORs.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.160
The what?

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:45.840
Roar Omega Roar.
The top fraternity on campus.

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:48.320
They only accept the highly elite.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.000
Okay, I'll lift the bed, you grab the pig.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.560
-Ready? One, two, three.
-What? No, no... Oh! What...

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:53.280
That's it. Don't let go.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:54.600
-Careful. He's a biter.
-(MIKE WHIMPERING)

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:56.160
(SCREAMS)

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.960
Whoa! Whoa, hey... (YELPS) Whoa!

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.360
-(GROANS)
-(SQUEALING)

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:02.520
I got him!

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:04.280
Uh-oh! Whoa!

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:07.040
(CHUCKLES)

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.880
That was awesome!

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:11.920
What am I doing? James P. Sullivan.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.480
Mike Wazowski.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.440
Listen, it was quite delightful
meeting you

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:16.720
and whatever that is,

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:18.880
but if you don't mind,
I have to study my Scaring.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:20.560
(BLOWS RASPBERRY)
You don't need to study Scaring.

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:21.720
You just do it.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:24.400
Really? I think there's
a little more to it than that.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.200
But, hey, thanks for stopping by.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:27.680
(GASPS) Let go of that!

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:30.480
-My hat!
-My pig!

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:32.040
(CHUCKLING)

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:33.120
Ooh!

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:35.840
Hey! Come here!

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:38.080
-Hey!
-(CONTINUES CHUCKLING)

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:39.200
Catch it!

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:41.360
Come back here!

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:43.560
-Ooh! Yeah!
-(SCREAMS)

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:45.360
Ride it to frat row!

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:47.920
(YELPING)

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.360
♪ Tentacles and serpent's wings,
they... ♪

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:51.440
Hey!

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.280
Whoa... Ow!

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:56.080
(CROWD CHATTERING)

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:57.440
(MONSTER WHOOPING)

00:05:57.880 --> 00:05:59.400
(YELPING)

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.000
Wow!

00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:03.320
(ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:05.840
-(WHOOPING)
-Whoa!

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:07.280
(CHUCKLES)

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:09.120
-Go, go, go!
-(SCREAMS)

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:10.200
Hey...

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:12.520
-Come on! Hey!
-Ooh!

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:13.640
Cupcake?

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:14.840
-(SCREAMS)
-(GASPS)

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.920
(GROANS)

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.240
Whoa...

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:20.440
(GRUNTS)

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:22.440
(SULLEY LAUGHING)

